{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasisCore","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasisCore","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Basis.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Dimension.StrongRankCondition","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Finsupp.VectorSpace","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Fintype.EquivFin","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Fintype.OfMap","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Finset.Max","lean:module:Mathlib.GroupTheory.GroupAction.FixingSubgroup","lean:module:Mathlib.GroupTheory.Complement","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.StandardYoungTableau","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.Specht","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Group"],"declarations":115,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.standardPolytabloid_span","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.standardPolytabloid_span","kind":"theorem","line":3029,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtStandardBasisCore.lean#L3029-L3038","doc":"**Content obligation 2/2 — spanning**, now derived **sorry-free** (the M^μ span\nidentity + the corestriction to `⊤` in `S^μ` are discharged here). Keeps the original\nname/signature for `Basis.mk`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.standardPolytabloid_span_eq_specht","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.standardPolytabloid_span_eq_specht","kind":"theorem","line":3016,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtStandardBasisCore.lean#L3016-L3027","doc":"**M^μ-level span identity.** The standard polytabloids span exactly `S^μ`\ninside `M^μ`. (≤): each standard polytabloid is a polytabloid (`standardPolytabloid_mem`);\n(≥): the straightening core. Sorry-free. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.standardPolytabloid_straightening","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.standardPolytabloid_straightening","kind":"theorem","line":2989,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtStandardBasisCore.lean#L2989-L3014","doc":"**Spanning half — proved sorry-free.** Every polytabloid `e_t` (arbitrary tableau `t`)\nlies in the\nspan of the *standard* polytabloids, by well-founded (strong) induction on the\n**column-word measure** `colWordNum t` (DESCENDING): if `e_t` is already a standard\npolytabloid it is in the spanning set; otherwise `straightening_step` rewrites it\nover tableaux of strictly *smaller* `colWordNum`, each in the span by the induction\nhypothesis, and the span is closed under `k`-linear combinations. (The measure is\n`colWordNum`, not `domWeight`: `domWeight` — tabloid dominance — cannot drive this\ninduction, since Garnir produces dominance-incomparable terms; see the audit doc.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.straightening_step","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.straightening_step","kind":"theorem","line":2943,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtStandardBasisCore.lean#L2943-L2987","doc":"**Straightening step (Sagan §2.6) — reduced sorry-free to the column-maximal core.**\nA polytabloid `e_t` that is *not itself* a standard polytabloid is a `k`-linear\ncombination of polytabloids of **strictly `colWordNum`-smaller** tableaux (the\nvalidated column-word measure). From this core, the full spanning half\n(`standardPolytabloid_straightening`) follows sorry-free by well-founded induction on\n`colWordNum t` (descending).\n\n**Reduction (sorry-free half).** Split on whether some column permutation `σ ∈ C_t`\nstrictly *lowers* `colWordNum` (equivalently: `t`'s columns are not yet sorted):\n\n* **Column-lowering** (`∃ σ ∈ C_t, colWordNum (σ•t) < colWordNum t`) — handled here\n  outright by the column-antisymmetry lever `polytabloid_colStab_smul`: since\n  `e_{σ•t} = sgn(σ)·e_t` and `sgn(σ)² = 1`, we get `e_t = sgn(σ)·e_{σ•t}`, a\n  one-term combination over `{σ•t}`, and `colWordNum (σ•t) < colWordNum t` is exactly\n  the branch hypothesis. No dominance theory needed.\n* **Column-word-minimal** (no such `σ`, i.e. columns sorted) — delegated to\n  `straightening_step_colMax`, the single Garnir residual, which carries the\n  hypothesis `hmax` that no column permutation lowers `colWordNum`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.straightening_step_colMax","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.straightening_step_colMax","kind":"theorem","line":2850,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtStandardBasisCore.lean#L2850-L2941","doc":"**The residual straightening core, on the CORRECT `colWordNum` measure\n(Sagan §2.6 Garnir relations).**\nA polytabloid `e_t` that is *not itself* a standard polytabloid **and** whose tableau\n`t` is already **column-word-minimal** — no column permutation `σ ∈ C_t` *lowers* the\ncolumn-word measure `colWordNum` (hypothesis `hmax`: `colWordNum t ≤ colWordNum (σ•t)`\nfor all `σ`, i.e. `t`'s columns are already sorted) — is a `k`-linear combination of\npolytabloids of **strictly `colWordNum`-smaller** tableaux.\n\nThis restatement replaces the earlier `domWeight`-based version, which was **false**\n(exact-arithmetic disproof, μ=(3,2), t=[[1,2,3],[5,4]]; audit §3.5): `domWeight`\n(tabloid dominance) cannot order the Garnir terms because they are dominance-\n*incomparable* to `{t}`. The **column-word** measure does order them — every\nnon-identity Garnir term is strictly `colWordNum`-smaller (validated exhaustively to\nshape (3,3,2)/(4,3,1); audit §4.5). This theorem is therefore now a TRUE statement.\n\nThis is the *irreducible* combinatorial heart of the straightening algorithm with the\n**column-sort already exhausted**: because `hmax` says no column permutation lowers\n`colWordNum` further (columns sorted), the column-antisymmetry lever\n`polytabloid_colStab_smul` is spent, and closing this requires the **Garnir coset-sum\nidentity at a row descent** (Sagan §2.6) — proved sorry-free below\n(`garnir_full_annihilation`, `sum_over_garnirG_reindex`, `transversal_sum_eq_zero`,\n`garnir_transversal_exists`, `sum_sign_rep_polytabloid_eq_zero_of_family`) — plus the\nnew **column-word decrease** lemma. The general `straightening_step` reduces to this\ncase sorry-free by splitting on whether a `colWordNum`-lowering column permutation\nexists.\n\n`hmax` is a genuine restriction (a column-word-minimal `t` is column-standard), so\nthis is an honest sub-case: for a column-standard non-standard `t` a row descent\nbetween adjacent columns exists and the Garnir relation yields strictly\n`colWordNum`-smaller terms. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.fibre_colWordNum_decrease","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.fibre_colWordNum_decrease","kind":"theorem","line":2771,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtStandardBasisCore.lean#L2771-L2846","doc":"**Fibre-decrease capstone (sorry-free).** For a column-word-minimal `t` at a row descent\n`(i,j)/(i,j+1)` and a genuine Garnir fibre `π ∈ garnirG \\ garnirH`, the column-sorted image\n`ρ•(π•t)` (from `exists_colWordMin_form`) is strictly `colWordNum`-smaller than `t`. Column\n`j` decreases pointwise (count-domination `fibre_colContent_j_count_dom` →\n`orderEmbOfFin_le_of_count` → `labelAt_eq_orderStat`), strictly at the top-most changed row\n(`fibre_colContent_j_ne` → `exists_first_lt_of_le_of_ne`), columns `< j` are untouched\n(`colContent_garnirG_eq_of_lt`), and `colWordNum_lt_of_first_diff_col` closes it. This is the\n`hgood` the straightening assembly needs. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.fibre_colContent_j_ne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.fibre_colContent_j_ne","kind":"theorem","line":2727,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtStandardBasisCore.lean#L2727-L2768","doc":"**A genuine Garnir fibre changes column `j`'s content (sorry-free).** For `π ∈ garnirG`\nwith `π ∉ garnirH` (a non-column-preserving coset element), `colContent (π•t) j ≠ colContent\nt j`. Contrapositive of `colStab_of_garnirA_image_eq`: equal column-`j` content forces\n`garnirA.image π = garnirA` (cancel the common above-descent part `P`), hence `π ∈ colStab t`,\nhence `π ∈ garnirH` — excluded. Supplies the strict row for `exists_first_lt_of_le_of_ne`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.colStab_of_garnirA_image_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.colStab_of_garnirA_image_eq","kind":"theorem","line":2664,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtStandardBasisCore.lean#L2664-L2724","doc":"**`garnirA` fixed setwise ⇒ column stabiliser (sorry-free).** If `π ∈ garnirG` maps\n`garnirA` onto itself, then it maps `garnirB` onto itself (card argument on `A∪B`) and fixes\nthe complement of `A∪B`, so it preserves the whole column pattern: `π ∈ C_t`. This is the\nconverse used for the fibre strictness — a fibre that leaves column `j`'s content unchanged\nis a column permutation, hence lies in `garnirH` (excluded for a genuine Garnir term). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.garnirG_image_AB","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.garnirG_image_AB","kind":"theorem","line":2646,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtStandardBasisCore.lean#L2646-L2661","doc":"**A Garnir element maps `A∪B` onto itself (sorry-free).** `π ∈ garnirG` fixes every label\noutside `A∪B` and is a bijection, so it permutes `A∪B`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.colContent_smul_j_split","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.colContent_smul_j_split","kind":"theorem","line":2623,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtStandardBasisCore.lean#L2623-L2643","doc":"**Fibre column-`j` content decomposition (sorry-free).** For `π ∈ garnirG`, `colContent\n(π•t) j` is `P` (unchanged — `π` fixes it) union the `π`-image of `garnirA`'s value set. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.colContent_j_split","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.colContent_j_split","kind":"theorem","line":2611,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtStandardBasisCore.lean#L2611-L2620","doc":"**Column-`j` content decomposition (sorry-free).** `colContent t j` is the (disjoint)\nunion of the above-descent value set `P` and the `garnirA` value set. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.colj_labelset_split","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.colj_labelset_split","kind":"theorem","line":2596,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtStandardBasisCore.lean#L2596-L2608","doc":"Column `j`'s labels split into the above-descent part (rows `< i`) and `garnirA`\n(rows `≥ i`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.fibre_colContent_j_count_dom","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.fibre_colContent_j_count_dom","kind":"theorem","line":2493,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtStandardBasisCore.lean#L2493-L2593","doc":"**Fibre column-`j` count-domination (sorry-free) — the order-statistics heart.** At a\nGarnir row descent of a column-word-minimal `t`, the column-`j` content of the raw fibre\n`π•t` count-dominates that of `t`: for every `w`, `colContent t j` has no more elements\n`≤ w` than `colContent (π•t) j`. Reason: both share the fixed above-descent part `P`\n(column `j`, rows `< i`, which `π` fixes); the changing part is `A = garnirA` for `t` versus\n`S = π(A)` for `π•t`, and since **every** `B`-label is `< ` every `A`-label\n(`garnir_B_lt_A`), `A` is the *top-`|A|`* subset of `A∪B`, so any `|A|`-subset `S ⊆ A∪B`\ncount-dominates it (`count_dom_of_top`); adding the common `P` preserves this\n(`filter_le_card_union_mono`). Via `orderStat_le_of_count_ge` this is exactly\n`labelAt (π•t sorted) (r,j) ≤ labelAt t (r,j)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.colContent_garnirG_eq_of_lt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.colContent_garnirG_eq_of_lt","kind":"theorem","line":2470,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtStandardBasisCore.lean#L2470-L2490","doc":"**A Garnir element fixes the content of every column left of `j` (sorry-free).** For\n`π ∈ S_{A∪B}` (`garnirG`), a column `c < j` holds only labels *outside* `A∪B` (`A` is in\ncolumn `j`, `B` in `j+1`), so `π` fixes them pointwise and `colContent (π•t) c = colContent t\nc`. Combined with `colContent_colStab_eq` + `labelAt_eq_of_colContent_eq`, this discharges\n`colWordNum_lt_of_first_diff_col`'s `hleft`: the fibre and `t` agree on every cell to the\nleft of the Garnir columns. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.sum_over_garnirG_reindex","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.sum_over_garnirG_reindex","kind":"theorem","line":2444,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtStandardBasisCore.lean#L2444-L2465","doc":"**Coset reindexing (sorry-free) — Garnir bridge, reindex step.** For any transversal\n`T` whose product family `{π·ρ : π ∈ T, ρ ∈ H}` covers `garnirG` bijectively (encoded by\nthe two inclusions + the cardinality match), a sum over `garnirG` reindexes as the double\nsum `∑_{π∈T} ∑_{ρ∈H}`. Purely `Finset`-level (image + injectivity-from-cardinality); this\nturns `garnir_full_annihilation` into `transversal_sum_eq_zero`'s `hann`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.garnir_transversal_with_pivot","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.garnir_transversal_with_pivot","kind":"theorem","line":2395,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtStandardBasisCore.lean#L2395-L2441","doc":"**Garnir transversal with a distinguished `H`-pivot (sorry-free).** Strengthens\n`garnir_transversal_exists`: since `T` is a *transversal* of the subgroup `H = garnirH`, it\ncontains exactly one element of `H` — the pivot `π₀` (the `H`-coset representative,\nextracted by factoring `1 ∈ garnirG` through the product bijection). Every *other* `T`-element\nis `∉ garnirH`, so it is a genuine Garnir fibre and `fibre_colWordNum_decrease` applies. `π₀`\nserves as `garnir_assembly_gen`'s `π₀` (its `hfix` holds because `π₀ ∈ garnirH ⊆ colStab`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.garnir_transversal_exists","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.garnir_transversal_exists","kind":"theorem","line":2343,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtStandardBasisCore.lean#L2343-L2392","doc":"**Garnir transversal existence (sorry-free).** A left transversal `T` of `H` in `G`\nwhose product family `{π·ρ}` covers `garnirG` bijectively — the exact hypotheses\n`sum_over_garnirG_reindex` consumes.  Built from Mathlib's `exists_left_transversal_of_le`\nthrough the subgroup-carrier bridges `garnirGSub_coe`/`garnirHSub_coe`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.garnirHSub_coe","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.garnirHSub_coe","kind":"theorem","line":2333,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtStandardBasisCore.lean#L2333-L2340","doc":"The subgroup `garnirHSub`'s carrier equals the `Finset` `garnirH` as sets. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.garnirGSub_coe","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.garnirGSub_coe","kind":"theorem","line":2325,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtStandardBasisCore.lean#L2325-L2330","doc":"The subgroup `garnirGSub`'s carrier equals the `Finset` `garnirG` as sets. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.garnirHSub_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.garnirHSub_le","kind":"theorem","line":2319,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtStandardBasisCore.lean#L2319-L2322","doc":"`H ≤ G` at the subgroup level — the input to `exists_left_transversal_of_le`\nfor the (future) coset-transversal reindexing. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.garnirHSub","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.garnirHSub","kind":"def","line":2314,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtStandardBasisCore.lean#L2314-L2316","doc":"`H = S_A × S_B` as a `Subgroup`: the elements of `garnirGSub` preserving columns. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.mem_garnirGSub","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.mem_garnirGSub","kind":"theorem","line":2302,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtStandardBasisCore.lean#L2302-L2312","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.garnirGSub","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.garnirGSub","kind":"def","line":2294,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtStandardBasisCore.lean#L2294-L2299","doc":"`S_{A∪B}` as a genuine `Subgroup` (via `fixingSubgroup` of the complement of\n`A ∪ B`), for the coset-transversal reindexing that connects `garnir_full_annihilation`\nto `garnir_assembly`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.garnir_H_sum_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.garnir_H_sum_eq","kind":"theorem","line":2272,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtStandardBasisCore.lean#L2272-L2292","doc":"**The `H`-part of the Garnir sum collapses to `|H|·e_t` (sorry-free).** Every\n`σ ∈ H = S_A × S_B ⊆ C_t` acts on `e_t` by its sign (column antisymmetry\n`polytabloid_colStab_smul` composed with equivariance `polytabloid_rep_smul`), so the\nsigned term `sgn(σ)·(σ·e_t) = sgn(σ)²·e_t = e_t`. Summing over `H` gives `|H|` copies.\nThis isolates `e_t` from `garnir_full_annihilation` for the full-group straightening path\n(see the audit doc §5.1): `|H|·e_t = −∑_{σ ∈ garnirG \\ H} sgn(σ)·(σ·e_t)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.garnirH_card_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.garnirH_card_pos","kind":"theorem","line":2260,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtStandardBasisCore.lean#L2260-L2269","doc":"`0 < |H|` — the identity lies in the Garnir subgroup. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.garnirH_subset_colStab","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.garnirH_subset_colStab","kind":"theorem","line":2252,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtStandardBasisCore.lean#L2252-L2257","doc":"`H ⊆ C_t` — every Garnir-subgroup element preserves columns. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.garnirH","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.garnirH","kind":"def","line":2245,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtStandardBasisCore.lean#L2245-L2249","doc":"The Garnir subgroup `H = S_A × S_B`: the elements of `S_{A∪B}` that additionally\npreserve every column of `t` (so they permute within `A` and within `B` separately).\nRealised as `garnirG ∩ C_t`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.garnir_full_annihilation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.garnir_full_annihilation","kind":"theorem","line":2208,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtStandardBasisCore.lean#L2208-L2243","doc":"**Garnir full-set annihilation (sorry-free).** The rep-level signed sum over\n`S_{A∪B}` annihilates `e_t`.  For every `ρ ∈ C_t` the pigeonhole\n(`garnir_row_collision`) supplies a same-row transposition `τ_ρ = swap a b` of\n`A ∪ B` labels; `mtab_sum_sign_smul_of_eq_zero` then kills the tabloid family, and\n`sum_sign_rep_polytabloid_eq_zero_of_family` lifts it to the polytabloid. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.garnirG","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.garnirG","kind":"def","line":2201,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtStandardBasisCore.lean#L2201-L2205","doc":"The Garnir permutation set `S_{A∪B}`: permutations fixing every label outside\n`A ∪ B`.  A subgroup (as a `Finset`) closed under right-multiplication by any\ntransposition of two labels of `A ∪ B`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.garnir_B_lt_A","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.garnir_B_lt_A","kind":"theorem","line":2144,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtStandardBasisCore.lean#L2144-L2199","doc":"**`B < A` entirely (sorry-free) — the foundation of the fibre-decrease bound.**\nAt a Garnir row descent — `labelAt t hij1 ≤ labelAt t hij`, i.e. in label order the\ncol-`j+1` entry at row `i` is `≤` the col-`j` entry at row `i` — of a column-word-minimal\n(hence column-standard) `t`, **every** label `b ∈ B` (col `j+1`, rows `≤ i`) is strictly\nsmaller (in label order) than **every** label `a ∈ A` (col `j`, rows `≥ i`). Reason:\ncolumn-standardness gives `b ≤ labelAt(i,j+1)` (b at row `≤ i` in col `j+1`) and\n`labelAt(i,j) ≤ a` (a at row `≥ i` in col `j`), while the descent + label-distinctness give\n`labelAt(i,j+1) < labelAt(i,j)`. This is why any non-identity fibre — which moves a\n`B`-label into column `j` — strictly lowers `colWordNum`: column `j` precedes column `j+1`\nin the column-major reading, so a smaller label entering column `j`'s cells lowers a more\nsignificant digit of the base-`(n+1)` word. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.garnirB","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.garnirB","kind":"def","line":2139,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtStandardBasisCore.lean#L2139-L2141","doc":"The Garnir label-set `B`: labels in column `j+1` of `t` at rows `≤ i`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.garnirA","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.garnirA","kind":"def","line":2135,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtStandardBasisCore.lean#L2135-L2137","doc":"The Garnir label-set `A`: labels in column `j` of `t` at rows `≥ i`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.garnir_row_collision","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.garnir_row_collision","kind":"theorem","line":2024,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtStandardBasisCore.lean#L2024-L2133","doc":"**Garnir pigeonhole (sorry-free) — the row collision for `hfam`.**\nAt a row descent `(i,j),(i,j+1) ∈ μ`, for *every* column permutation `ρ ∈ C_t` there\nare two distinct labels — one in `A` (column `j`, row `≥ i`) and one in `B`\n(column `j+1`, row `≤ i`) — that land in the **same row** of `ρ • t`.\n\nProof: `|A| = colLen j − i`, `|B| = i+1`, so `|A ∪ B| = colLen j + 1`; the map\n`l ↦ rowPattern (ρ•t) l = rowPattern t (ρ⁻¹ l)` sends `A ∪ B` into\n`{0, …, colLen j − 1}` (`ρ ∈ C_t` keeps `ρ⁻¹ l` in its column; `colLen (j+1) ≤ colLen j`),\na set of size `colLen j`, so two elements collide. Column-injectivity of the map rules\nout both being in `A` or both in `B`, so the colliding pair straddles `A` and `B`. This\nis exactly the same-row transposition `τ_ρ ∈ rowStab (ρ•t) ∩ S_{A∪B}` that\n`mtab_sum_sign_smul_of_eq_zero` consumes to discharge `hfam ρ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.card_col_labels_row_lt_of_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.card_col_labels_row_lt_of_le","kind":"theorem","line":1994,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtStandardBasisCore.lean#L1994-L2021","doc":"The labels in column `c` of `t` with row index `< m` number exactly `m`, provided\n`m ≤ μ.colLen c` (they biject with rows `0, …, m-1`, all of which occur in column `c`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.colContent_eq_of_labelAt_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.colContent_eq_of_labelAt_eq","kind":"theorem","line":1969,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtStandardBasisCore.lean#L1969-L1991","doc":"**Equal cell labels ⇒ equal column content (sorry-free).** Converse of\n`labelAt_eq_of_colContent_eq`: two column-word-minimal tableaux whose column-`c` cell labels\nagree at every row have the *same* column-`c` content — the two increasing enumerations\ncoincide, so (via `range_orderEmbOfFin`) their ranges, hence the finsets, coincide. Supplies\nthe `f ≠ g` (strictness) input from `colContent (π•t) j ≠ colContent t j`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.labelAt_eq_of_colContent_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.labelAt_eq_of_colContent_eq","kind":"theorem","line":1950,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtStandardBasisCore.lean#L1950-L1966","doc":"**Equal column content ⇒ equal cell labels (sorry-free).** Two column-word-minimal\n(hence column-standard) tableaux with the *same* column-`c` content have the *same* label at\nevery cell `(r, c)` — both are the increasing enumeration of that content\n(`labelAt_eq_orderStat`), and `orderEmbOfFin` depends only on the finset. This is the lemma\nthat turns \"the fibre and `t` share a column's content\" into \"they agree cell-by-cell on\nthat column\" — supplying both the `hleft` (columns left of `j`) and the strict-row\ncomparison for `colWordNum_lt_of_first_diff_col`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.colContent_colStab_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.colContent_colStab_eq","kind":"theorem","line":1925,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtStandardBasisCore.lean#L1925-L1947","doc":"**A column permutation preserves every column's content (sorry-free).** If `ρ ∈ C_t`\n(fixes the column pattern) then `colContent (ρ•t) c = colContent t c` for every column `c`.\nThe column-sort `ρ` that produces the column-word-minimal image of a fibre `π•t` therefore\nleaves each `colContent (π•t) c` unchanged — which is what lets `labelAt_eq_orderStat` read\nthe sorted image's cell labels off the (unsorted) fibre's column content. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.colContent_smul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.colContent_smul","kind":"theorem","line":1904,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtStandardBasisCore.lean#L1904-L1922","doc":"**Column content under the `S_n`-action (sorry-free).** The action `σ • t = σ.symm.trans\nt` sends the label at cell `c` to `σ` of the old label (`colPattern (σ•t) l = colPattern t\n(σ.symm l)`), so column `j`'s content of `σ•t` is the `σ`-image of column `j`'s labels of\n`t`. For the Garnir fibre element `σ`, this is exactly the reindexing that turns the abstract\n`A∪B` shuffle into the concrete `colContent (σ•t) j`, feeding `count_dom_of_top`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.labelAt_eq_orderStat","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.labelAt_eq_orderStat","kind":"theorem","line":1849,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtStandardBasisCore.lean#L1849-L1901","doc":"**Cell label = order statistic (sorry-free).** For a column-word-minimal (hence\ncolumn-standard, `colStandard_of_colWordMin`) tableau `t`, the label sitting at cell\n`(r, j)` is the `r`-th smallest label of column `j` — reading a sorted column\ntop-to-bottom enumerates `colContent t j` in increasing order. This is the\ntableau ↔ order-statistic bridge that lets the abstract `orderStat_le_of_count_ge`\ndomination be read off actual tableaux, feeding the column-word decrease bound. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.colContent_card","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.colContent_card","kind":"theorem","line":1839,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtStandardBasisCore.lean#L1839-L1846","doc":"**`colContent` cardinality (sorry-free).** Column `j` holds exactly `μ.colLen j`\nlabels; `Fin.val` is injective, so the image keeps that count. Supplies the\n`s.card = k` hypothesis for `orderEmbOfFin`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.colContent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.colContent","kind":"def","line":1830,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtStandardBasisCore.lean#L1830-L1836","doc":"**Column-`j` label content of a tableau, as a `Finset ℕ`** — the set of the labels\nsitting in column `j` (the image of the column-`j` label fibre under `Fin.val`). This is\nthe order-statistics substrate for the column-word decrease: the Garnir shuffle only\nchanges the *contents* of columns `j` and `j+1`, and the resulting column-word change is\ngoverned by how these `Finset ℕ` contents compare (`orderStat_le_of_count_ge`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.card_col_labels","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.card_col_labels","kind":"theorem","line":1807,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtStandardBasisCore.lean#L1807-L1827","doc":"The labels in column `c` of `t` number exactly `μ.colLen c` (they biject with the\ncells of `μ.col c` under the tableau equivalence `t`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.poly_combo_reindex","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.poly_combo_reindex","kind":"theorem","line":1770,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtStandardBasisCore.lean#L1770-L1798","doc":"**Reindex a polytabloid combination through per-term reductions (sorry-free).** If\n`e_t = ∑_{t'∈s} c_{t'} e_{t'}` and each `e_{t'}` equals a scalar multiple of some `e_u` with\n`colWordNum u < colWordNum t`, then `e_t` is a combination of *strictly `colWordNum`-smaller*\npolytabloids. This is the raw→sorted bookkeeping that upgrades `garnir_assembly_gen`'s output\n(terms `e_{π•t}` on the raw fibre) into the `straightening_step_colMax` conclusion (terms on\nthe column-sorted images `e_{ρ•(π•t)}`, each strictly smaller by `fibre_colWordNum_decrease`).\nSame fiberwise regrouping as `garnir_assembly_gen`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.garnir_assembly_gen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.garnir_assembly_gen","kind":"theorem","line":1714,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtStandardBasisCore.lean#L1714-L1767","doc":"**Garnir assembly, measure-generic (sorry-free).** The `domWeight`-free version of\n`garnir_assembly`: parametric over an arbitrary predicate `P : Tableau → Prop` classifying\nthe \"good\" (further-reducible or terminal) neighbours. Given a transversal `T ∋ π₀` with\nthe signed representation sum vanishing (`hann`) and every non-distinguished rep `π`\nlanding in `P` (`hgood`), the polytabloid `e_t` is a `k`-linear combination of\npolytabloids of tableaux all satisfying `P`. The reindexing (identity isolation →\n`sum_fiberwise` aggregation) is measure-agnostic; only the classifying predicate changes.\n\nThe `colWordNum` `straightening_step_colMax` instantiates this with\n`P t' := colWordNum t' < colWordNum t` (via `hgood` = the column-word-decrease bound). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.garnir_assembly","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.garnir_assembly","kind":"theorem","line":1642,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtStandardBasisCore.lean#L1642-L1711","doc":"**Garnir assembly (sorry-free) — the `domWeight`-era bookkeeping helper.**\nGiven a transversal `T ∋ π₀` for which (i) the signed representation sum vanishes\n(`hann` — the output of `transversal_sum_eq_zero`), and (ii) every *non-distinguished*\nrepresentative `π` strictly raises the dominance measure\n(`hdom : domWeight t < domWeight (π • t)`), the polytabloid `e_t` is a `k`-linear\ncombination of polytabloids of strictly `domWeight`-greater tabloids.\n\nPure bookkeeping: isolate the distinguished term `sgn(π₀)·(π₀·e_t) = ±e_t` from `hann`,\ngiving `e_t = ∑_{π ∈ T, π ≠ π₀} (−sgn π)·e_{π·t}` (via equivariance\n`polytabloid_rep_smul`), then reindex the permutation sum to a sum over the tableaux\n`{π·t}` with fibrewise-aggregated coefficients.\n\n**Orphaned by the 2026-07-07 measure correction.** `straightening_step_colMax` has been\nrestated over `colWordNum` (the `domWeight` version was FALSE — audit §3.5), so this\n`domWeight`-based assembly is NO LONGER on the straightening path and does not close the\ncurrent `colMax`. It is retained sorry-free (parallel to the orphaned `domWeight`/\n`domBound` scaffolding); the `colWordNum` colMax will want an analogous assembly whose\n`hdom` reads `colWordNum (π • t) < colWordNum t`. The *reindexing* argument here (identity\nisolation → `sum_image` fibre-aggregation) is measure-agnostic and transcribes directly. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.exists_row_descent_of_colWordMin","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.exists_row_descent_of_colWordMin","kind":"theorem","line":1608,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtStandardBasisCore.lean#L1608-L1639","doc":"**Pure row-descent existence under column-word-minimality (sorry-free) — the\n`colWordNum` analogue of `exists_row_descent_of_colMax`.** A column-word-minimal `t`\nwhose polytabloid is non-standard has a **row descent** (column descents are killed by\n`colStandard_of_colWordMin`). This is the row descent the `colWordNum` Garnir coset-sum\nstep of `straightening_step_colMax` consumes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.colStandard_of_colWordMin","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.colStandard_of_colWordMin","kind":"theorem","line":1584,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtStandardBasisCore.lean#L1584-L1605","doc":"**Column-standardness under column-word-minimality (sorry-free) — the `colWordNum`\nanalogue of `colStandard_of_colMax`.** If `t` is column-word-minimal (`hmax`: no\n`σ ∈ C_t` *lowers* `colWordNum`), then each column's labels strictly increase with the\nrow. A violation (`↑a < ↑b` same column but `rowPattern t b < rowPattern t a`) would be a\ncolumn descent, giving a `colWordNum`-*lowering* transposition (`colStab_swap_mem` +\n`colWordNum_swap_lt`) that contradicts `hmax`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.exists_row_descent_of_colMax","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.exists_row_descent_of_colMax","kind":"theorem","line":1548,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtStandardBasisCore.lean#L1548-L1582","doc":"**Pure row-descent existence under column-maximality (sorry-free).** Combines\n`exists_descent_of_not_mem_range` (a non-standard polytabloid has a row *or* column\ndescent) with `colStandard_of_colMax` (column-maximality kills column descents): a\ncolumn-maximal `t` whose polytabloid is non-standard has a **row descent**. This is\nexactly the input the Garnir coset-sum step of `straightening_step_colMax` consumes —\nit closes Garnir piece 1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.colStandard_of_colMax","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.colStandard_of_colMax","kind":"theorem","line":1522,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtStandardBasisCore.lean#L1522-L1545","doc":"**Column-standardness under column-maximality (sorry-free).** Combining steps 3b/3c:\nif `t` is column-(dominance-)maximal (`hmax`: no `σ ∈ C_t` raises `domWeight`), then the\nlabels in each column of `t` strictly increase with the row — `t` has **no column\ndescent**. Two same-column labels with `↑a < ↑b` have `rowPattern t a < rowPattern t b`;\na violation would give a `domWeight`-raising column transposition (`colStab_swap_mem` +\n`domWeight_swap_lt`) contradicting `hmax`. This is the exact \"column-sort exhausted\"\nconsequence the Garnir core `straightening_step_colMax` consumes: it leaves only pure\n*row* descents to resolve. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.domWeight_swap_lt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.domWeight_swap_lt","kind":"theorem","line":1455,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtStandardBasisCore.lean#L1455-L1520","doc":"**Garnir step 3c (sorry-free) — the dominance strict-increase core.** Swapping a\n*column descent* strictly raises `domWeight`: if the smaller label `a` (`↑a < ↑b`)\nsits in a strictly lower row than the larger label `b`\n(`rowPattern t b < rowPattern t a`), then the transposition `swap a b` — which moves\nthe smaller label up — strictly increases the dominance measure. The gap is exactly\n`(rowPattern t a − rowPattern t b) · (↑b − ↑a) ≥ 1`, realised termwise at\n`(i, m) = (rowPattern t b, ↑b)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.domCount'_two_point","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.domCount'_two_point","kind":"theorem","line":1436,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtStandardBasisCore.lean#L1436-L1453","doc":"**Two-point surgery for `domCount'`.** Splitting the underlying `card` sum at the\nlabels `a ≠ b` leaves a common tail (the sum over `univ \\ {a,b}`) plus the two\nindicator contributions of `a` and `b`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.rowPattern_lt_nOf","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.rowPattern_lt_nOf","kind":"theorem","line":1430,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtStandardBasisCore.lean#L1430-L1434","doc":"The row pattern of a tableau is bounded by `nOf μ`. Single copy (see\n`row_lt_card`); serves `SpechtDominanceCore` through its `open`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.row_lt_card","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.row_lt_card","kind":"theorem","line":1408,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtStandardBasisCore.lean#L1408-L1428","doc":"The row index of any cell of a Young diagram is `< ν.card` (the `i+1` cells\n`(0,0), …, (i,0)` lie in `ν` by down-closure). Single copy — downstream\n`SpechtDominanceCore` resolves to this declaration through its\n`open QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.colStab_swap_mem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.colStab_swap_mem","kind":"theorem","line":1394,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtStandardBasisCore.lean#L1394-L1406","doc":"**Garnir step 3b (sorry-free).** The transposition of two labels lying in the same\ncolumn of `t` stabilises the column pattern, hence lies in `C_t`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.exists_colWordMin_form","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.exists_colWordMin_form","kind":"theorem","line":1349,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtStandardBasisCore.lean#L1349-L1384","doc":"**Existence of a column-word-minimal form (sorry-free) — the `colsort` substitute.**\nEvery tableau `s` has a column permutation `ρ ∈ C_s` for which `ρ • s` is\n**column-word-minimal** (no `C_{ρ•s}` element lowers `colWordNum`) and\n`colWordNum (ρ • s) ≤ colWordNum s`. Since `ρ ∈ C_s`, `ρ • s` has the same\ncolumn-membership as `s` and `e_{ρ•s} = ±e_s` (column antisymmetry). This replaces an\nexplicit `colsort` **operation**: the sorted form is obtained by well-founded descent —\nif `s` is not already minimal, some `C_s`-element strictly lowers `colWordNum`, and the\ninduction hypothesis (strong induction on `colWordNum s`) supplies the minimal form of\nthat smaller tableau; column stabilisers compose via `colStab_smul_eq`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.colStab_smul_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.colStab_smul_eq","kind":"theorem","line":1339,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtStandardBasisCore.lean#L1339-L1347","doc":"**Column stabiliser is invariant under its own action (sorry-free).** If\n`σ ∈ C_s` (preserves `s`'s columns), then `σ • s` has the *same* column pattern as `s`,\nso `C_{σ•s} = C_s`. Used to compose column permutations while sorting. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.colWordNum_swap_lt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.colWordNum_swap_lt","kind":"theorem","line":1284,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtStandardBasisCore.lean#L1284-L1337","doc":"**Keystone (sorry-free): a within-column descent swap strictly lowers `colWordNum`.**\nIf labels `a < b` sit in the same column with `b` in an EARLIER row than `a` (a column\ndescent — the larger label higher up), swapping them strictly decreases the column-word\nmeasure. This is the `colWordNum` analogue of `domWeight_swap_lt`, and the lever the\n`straightening_step` column-lowering branch and the `colMax` row-descent argument will\nconsume. Proof: `cmajSig (t a) < cmajSig (t b)` (same column, `b` higher) gives\n`w a < w b` with `w m = (n+1)^{cmajSig (t m)}`; reindexing the swapped sum leaves only the\n`a,b` terms, and `b·w a + a·w b < a·w a + b·w b` is the rearrangement inequality. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.colWordNum_lt_of_first_diff_col","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.colWordNum_lt_of_first_diff_col","kind":"theorem","line":1263,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtStandardBasisCore.lean#L1263-L1282","doc":"**First-difference comparison in geometric (column-major) terms (sorry-free).** The\n`colWordNum_lt_of_first_diff` `hhigh` hypothesis, restated via `before_of_cmajSig_lt` in the\ntwo geometric conditions the fibre decrease actually supplies: `u` and `v` agree on every\ncell in a column strictly **left** of `c₀`'s column, and on every cell in `c₀`'s column\n**above** `c₀`; and `v` has a strictly smaller label at `c₀`. Then `colWordNum v <\ncolWordNum u`. For the Garnir fibre decrease `c₀` is the top-most cell of column `j` whose\nlabel changes; columns `< j` are untouched and column `j` above `c₀` is unchanged. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.colWordNum_lt_of_first_diff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.colWordNum_lt_of_first_diff","kind":"theorem","line":1182,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtStandardBasisCore.lean#L1182-L1260","doc":"**First-difference comparison for `colWordNum` (sorry-free).** If `u` and `v` agree\n(as labels) on every cell column-major-*earlier* than a cell `c₀` (i.e. `cmajSig` strictly\nlarger), and `v` has a strictly smaller label at `c₀`, then `colWordNum v < colWordNum u`.\nThis is the base-`(n+1)` \"most-significant differing digit decides\" principle, with\n`cmajSig` as the positional index. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.exists_first_lt_of_le_of_ne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.exists_first_lt_of_le_of_ne","kind":"theorem","line":1158,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtStandardBasisCore.lean#L1158-L1180","doc":"**First strict index of a pointwise-`≤`, unequal pair (sorry-free).** If `f ≤ g`\npointwise on `Fin N` and `f ≠ g`, there is a *least* index `r₀` with `f r₀ < g r₀`, below\nwhich `f` and `g` agree. Supplies `colWordNum_lt_of_first_diff_col`'s cell `c₀` (the\ntop-most changed row of the Garnir column) together with its `habove` (agreement above). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.filter_le_card_union_mono","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.filter_le_card_union_mono","kind":"theorem","line":1139,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtStandardBasisCore.lean#L1139-L1156","doc":"**Count-domination is preserved by adding a common disjoint part (sorry-free).** If `X`\nis count-dominated by `Y` (`≤ w` counts) and `P` is disjoint from both, then `P ∪ X` is\ncount-dominated by `P ∪ Y`. For the fibre decrease `P` is column `j`'s labels above the\ndescent row (fixed by the Garnir element), `X = A` (top-`|A|`), `Y = S = π(A)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.count_dom_of_top","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.count_dom_of_top","kind":"theorem","line":1103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtStandardBasisCore.lean#L1103-L1137","doc":"**Count-domination from the top-`|A|` structure (sorry-free).** If `A` is \"above\" `B`\n(every `b ∈ B` is below every `a ∈ A`) and `S ⊆ A ∪ B` has `|S| = |A|`, then for every\nthreshold `w` the top set `A` has no more elements `≤ w` than `S`. Feeds\n`orderStat_le_of_count_ge`: a Garnir fibre's column-`j` content `S` (a different `|A|`-subset\nof `A∪B`) sorted-dominates `t`'s content `A`, because `B < A` makes `A` the top subset. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.orderEmbOfFin_le_of_count","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.orderEmbOfFin_le_of_count","kind":"theorem","line":1091,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtStandardBasisCore.lean#L1091-L1101","doc":"**Order-statistic domination, common-`k` form (sorry-free).** `orderStat_le_of_count_ge`\nrestated with both finsets carrying a card proof to the *same* `k`, so the index `r : Fin k`\nmatches on both sides — the shape `labelAt_eq_orderStat` produces (`Fin (μ.colLen j)`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.orderEmbOfFin_congr","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.orderEmbOfFin_congr","kind":"theorem","line":1080,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtStandardBasisCore.lean#L1080-L1089","doc":"**`orderEmbOfFin` value is independent of the cardinality proof / index type\n(sorry-free).** For a fixed finset `s`, `s.orderEmbOfFin` at two indices with the same\n`ℕ`-value agrees — the increasing enumeration only depends on `s` and the position, not on\nwhich `s.card = k` proof presents the domain `Fin k`. Bridges `orderStat_le_of_count_ge`'s\n`Fin X.card` indexing to `labelAt_eq_orderStat`'s `Fin (colLen j)` indexing. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.orderStat_le_of_count_ge","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.orderStat_le_of_count_ge","kind":"theorem","line":1032,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtStandardBasisCore.lean#L1032-L1078","doc":"**Order-statistic domination (sorry-free).** If for every threshold `w` the finset `X`\nhas at least as many elements `≤ w` as `Y`, then `X`'s `r`-th smallest is `≤` `Y`'s `r`-th\nsmallest (`orderEmbOfFin` = the increasing enumeration). The order-theoretic core of the\nfibre-decrease: `B < A` makes `A` the top-`|A|` subset, so its column content dominates. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.card_fin_lt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.card_fin_lt","kind":"theorem","line":1019,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtStandardBasisCore.lean#L1019-L1030","doc":"`#{i : Fin n | (i:ℕ) < m} = m` for `m ≤ n` (sorry-free). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.card_fin_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.card_fin_le","kind":"theorem","line":1006,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtStandardBasisCore.lean#L1006-L1017","doc":"`#{i : Fin n | (i:ℕ) ≤ m} = m + 1` for `m < n` (sorry-free). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.digit_bound_indexed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.digit_bound_indexed","kind":"theorem","line":981,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtStandardBasisCore.lean#L981-L1004","doc":"**Indexed base-`B` digit bound (sorry-free):** distinct positions `e i < K`, digits\n`d i < B` ⇒ `∑ d i·B^{e i} < B^K`. The form the cell-indexed first-difference comparison\nconsumes (`e = cmajSig`, `d =` label). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.geom_digit_bound","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.geom_digit_bound","kind":"theorem","line":965,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtStandardBasisCore.lean#L965-L979","doc":"**Base-`B` digit bound (sorry-free):** a sum of digits `< B` at DISTINCT positions\n`< K` is `< B^K`. The arithmetic core of the \"most-significant differing cell\"\ncomparison. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.geom_sum_pred","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.geom_sum_pred","kind":"theorem","line":952,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtStandardBasisCore.lean#L952-L963","doc":"Geometric identity over ℕ: `(∑_{x<K} (B-1)·B^x) + 1 = B^K` for `1 ≤ B`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.before_of_cmajSig_lt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.before_of_cmajSig_lt","kind":"theorem","line":931,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtStandardBasisCore.lean#L931-L950","doc":"**Converse of `cmajSig` monotonicity (sorry-free).** Column-major order is linear, so a\nstrictly larger `cmajSig` forces the cell column-major-*before*: `cmajSig c₀ < cmajSig c`\ngives `c` precedes `c₀` (smaller column, or same column and smaller row). This is what\ndischarges the `hhigh` hypothesis of `colWordNum_lt_of_first_diff` — \"every\nhigher-significance cell agrees\" reduces to \"every column-major-earlier cell agrees\",\nwhich for the fibre decrease is \"cells in columns `< j`, and cells in column `j` above the\nfirst change\". ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.cmajSig_injOn","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.cmajSig_injOn","kind":"theorem","line":914,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtStandardBasisCore.lean#L914-L929","doc":"**`cmajSig` is injective on cells (sorry-free).** Distinct cells have distinct\nsignificance — column-major order is linear, so one cell strictly precedes the other and\nhas the strictly larger `cmajSig`. Makes `cmajSig` a bijection `μ.cells → {0,…,n-1}`, the\npositional index used by the base-`(n+1)` first-difference comparison. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.cmajSig_lt_of_before","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.cmajSig_lt_of_before","kind":"theorem","line":890,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtStandardBasisCore.lean#L890-L912","doc":"**`cmajSig` strict monotonicity, general column-major order (sorry-free).** If `c` is\ncolumn-major-*before* `c'` (lexicographic on `(col, row)`), then `cmajSig c' < cmajSig c`.\nGeneralises `cmajSig_lt_of_col_row` to cells in different columns. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.cmajSig_lt_of_col_row","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.cmajSig_lt_of_col_row","kind":"theorem","line":866,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtStandardBasisCore.lean#L866-L888","doc":"**`cmajSig` strict monotonicity (sorry-free).** Within one column (equal column\nindex), a cell in an EARLIER row is column-major-*before*, hence has strictly larger\n`cmajSig` (more cells come after it). The engine of `colWordNum_swap_lt`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.colWordNum_eq_cellSum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.colWordNum_eq_cellSum","kind":"theorem","line":852,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtStandardBasisCore.lean#L852-L864","doc":"**`colWordNum` as a sum over cells (sorry-free).** Reindexing the label-indexed\ndefinition through the tableau bijection `t`: `colWordNum t` is the total of\n`(label at cell c) · (n+1)^{cmajSig c}` over all cells `c`. The cell-indexed form is the\nnatural shape for the \"most-significant differing cell\" comparison. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.colWordNum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.colWordNum","kind":"def","line":844,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtStandardBasisCore.lean#L844-L850","doc":"The **column-word measure** of a tableau — the validated well-founded measure\nfor Garnir straightening (replaces the false-for-this-purpose `domWeight`). Reads\nthe labels in column-major cell order and encodes base `(n+1)` with the first\ncell most significant. Every non-identity Garnir straightening term has strictly\nsmaller `colWordNum`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.cmajSig","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.cmajSig","kind":"def","line":838,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtStandardBasisCore.lean#L838-L842","doc":"Column-major **significance exponent** of a cell `c`: the number of `μ`-cells\nstrictly LATER in column-major order (compare column index first, then row). The\nfirst column-major cell (top of the leftmost column) has the highest exponent. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.domWeight_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.domWeight_le","kind":"theorem","line":808,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtStandardBasisCore.lean#L808-L819","doc":"`domWeight t ≤ domBound μ` (sum of `(n+1)²` counts, each `≤ n`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.domCount'_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.domCount'_le","kind":"theorem","line":800,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtStandardBasisCore.lean#L800-L806","doc":"Each dominance count is bounded by `n = nOf μ` (a filtered subset of the\n`n`-element label set). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.domBound","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.domBound","kind":"def","line":795,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtStandardBasisCore.lean#L795-L798","doc":"A fixed ceiling for `domWeight` (used to run the strong induction on the\ndecreasing measure `domBound μ - domWeight t`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.domWeight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.domWeight","kind":"def","line":787,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtStandardBasisCore.lean#L787-L793","doc":"The **dominance weight** of a tableau: the total of all clamped dominance\ncounts of its row pattern. A strictly-monotone linear extension of the dominance\norder (a Garnir straightening step strictly increases it), hence a valid\nwell-founded measure for the straightening induction. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.domCount'","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.domCount'","kind":"def","line":782,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtStandardBasisCore.lean#L782-L785","doc":"The **dominance count** of a row pattern `f` (self-contained, local to this\nfile): `domCount' f i m = #{l : (l:ℕ) < m ∧ f l ≤ i}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.sum_sign_rep_polytabloid_eq_zero_of_family","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.sum_sign_rep_polytabloid_eq_zero_of_family","kind":"theorem","line":738,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtStandardBasisCore.lean#L738-L768","doc":"**Polytabloid annihilation from a tabloid-annihilation family (sorry-free) —\nGarnir piece 2, annihilation reduction.** The rep-level signed sum\n`∑_{σ ∈ G} sgn(σ)·(σ·e_t)` vanishes as soon as, for *every* column-stabiliser element\n`ρ ∈ C_t`, the tabloid-level signed sum `∑_{σ ∈ G} sgn(σ)·{σ·ρ·t}` vanishes (`hfam`).\n\nPure linear algebra: expand `e_t = ∑_{ρ ∈ C_t} sgn(ρ)·{ρ·t}`, push `rep σ` through\n(`rep_of`: `σ·{ρ·t} = {σ·ρ·t}`), swap the `G`- and `C_t`-sums, and factor out `sgn(ρ)`\nso each inner sum is exactly a term of `hfam`. This is the bridge from the tabloid-level\nGarnir annihilation (`mtab_sum_sign_smul_of_eq_zero`, applied to each `ρ·t` with a\nsame-row transposition of the Garnir set) to `transversal_sum_eq_zero`'s `hann`\nhypothesis — isolating the remaining pigeonhole crux entirely inside `hfam`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.transversal_sum_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.transversal_sum_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":700,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtStandardBasisCore.lean#L700-L735","doc":"**Transversal annihilation (sorry-free) — Garnir piece 2, bridge step 2.**\nGiven a set `H ⊆ C_t` with `0 < |H|` (the `S_A × S_B` factor) and a transversal `T`\n(coset representatives), *if* the signed group-action sum over the full product family\n`{π·ρ : π ∈ T, ρ ∈ H}` vanishes (hypothesis `hann` — supplied by the tabloid-level\nGarnir annihilation `mtab_sum_sign_smul_of_eq_zero` / `sum_sign_rep_eq_zero_of_fixed`\nonce the Garnir set is built), then the *transversal* signed sum vanishes:\n`∑_{π ∈ T} sgn(π)·(π·e_t) = 0`.\n\nThe `|H|` factor produced by collapsing each coset (`sum_sign_rep_coset_collapse`)\nis cancelled using `CharZero` — this is where dividing by `|S_A × S_B|` enters. The\nfinal Garnir relation `e_t = −∑_{π ≠ 1} sgn(π)·e_{π·t}` then follows by isolating the\nidentity coset representative. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.sum_sign_rep_coset_collapse","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.sum_sign_rep_coset_collapse","kind":"theorem","line":664,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtStandardBasisCore.lean#L664-L698","doc":"**Coset antisymmetriser collapse (sorry-free) — Garnir piece 2, bridge step 1.**\nFactoring the representation of a fixed `π` out of an inner signed sum over a set\n`H ⊆ C_t`: since every `ρ ∈ H` fixes `e_t` up to its sign\n(`rep_polytabloid_of_mem_colStab`), the signed sum over the *left-translated* family\n`{π·ρ : ρ ∈ H}` collapses to `sgn(π)·|H|·(π·e_t)`.\n\nThis is the inner-antisymmetriser step of the Garnir coset decomposition\n`S_{A∪B} = ⊔_π π·(S_A × S_B)`: within each coset the `S_A × S_B` factor (a subgroup of\n`C_t`) collapses via `sum_sign_rep_polytabloid`, leaving a single `±π·e_t` per coset\nrepresentative `π`. Summing this identity over a transversal is the next bridge step. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.sum_sign_rep_eq_zero_of_fixed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.sum_sign_rep_eq_zero_of_fixed","kind":"theorem","line":625,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtStandardBasisCore.lean#L625-L661","doc":"**Polytabloid-level Garnir annihilation (sorry-free).** The `rep`-level analog\nof `mtab_sum_sign_smul_of_eq_zero`: if a `sign(-1)` involution `τ` *fixes the\npolytabloid* (`τ · e_t = e_t`) and `G` is right-`τ`-closed, the signed group-action\nsum vanishes, `∑_{g∈G} sgn(g) · (g · e_t) = 0`. Same sign-reversing-involution\npairing `g ↔ gτ`: `rep(gτ)(e_t) = rep(g)(rep(τ)(e_t)) = rep(g)(e_t)` while\n`sgn(gτ) = -sgn(g)`. Once a row descent supplies such a `τ` (fixing `e_t` because\nit lies in a row after the Garnir swap), this is the Garnir relation\n`g_{A,B} · e_t = 0` at the polytabloid level. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.sum_sign_rep_polytabloid","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.sum_sign_rep_polytabloid","kind":"theorem","line":601,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtStandardBasisCore.lean#L601-L622","doc":"**Antisymmetriser eigenvalue (sorry-free).** Summing the signed group action\nover any finite set `H` of column-stabiliser elements collapses to `|H| · e_t`:\n`∑_{ρ∈H} sgn(ρ) · (ρ · e_t) = |H| · e_t`, because each term is\n`sgn(ρ)·sgn(ρ)·e_t = e_t` by the sign-eigenvector property (`sgn(ρ)² = 1`). This\nis the `α · e_t = |S_A×S_B| · e_t` step of the Garnir coset→polytabloid bridge\n(here for an arbitrary `H ⊆ C_t`, of which `S_A×S_B` is the relevant instance). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.rep_polytabloid_of_mem_colStab","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.rep_polytabloid_of_mem_colStab","kind":"theorem","line":588,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtStandardBasisCore.lean#L588-L598","doc":"**Polytabloid is a sign-eigenvector of its column stabiliser (sorry-free).**\nFor `σ ∈ C_t`, the representation acts on `e_t` by the sign character:\n`σ · e_t = sgn(σ) · e_t`. Immediate from equivariance\n(`polytabloid_rep_smul`: `e_{σ·t} = σ · e_t`) composed with column-antisymmetry\n(`polytabloid_colStab_smul`: `e_{σ·t} = sgn(σ) · e_t` for `σ ∈ C_t`). This is the\neigenvector property the Garnir antisymmetriser bridge consumes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.polytabloid_rep_smul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.polytabloid_rep_smul","kind":"theorem","line":538,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtStandardBasisCore.lean#L538-L585","doc":"**Polytabloid equivariance (sorry-free).** The polytabloid is `Sₙ`-equivariant:\n`e_{σ·t} = σ · e_t`, i.e. acting on the tableau by `σ` equals acting on the\npolytabloid by the module representation `Mtab.rep`. Reindex the column-stabiliser\nsum by the conjugation `π ↦ σπσ⁻¹` (bijecting `C_t ≅ C_{σ·t}`, preserving sign,\nand sending `σ·(π·t)` to `(σπσ⁻¹)·(σ·t)`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.mem_colStab_smul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.mem_colStab_smul","kind":"theorem","line":522,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtStandardBasisCore.lean#L522-L535","doc":"**Column-stabiliser conjugation.** `ρ ∈ C_{σ·t} ↔ σ⁻¹ρσ ∈ C_t` — the column\nstabiliser transforms by conjugation under the `Sₙ` action, since\n`colPattern (σ·t) = σ · colPattern t`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.mtab_sum_sign_smul_of_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.mtab_sum_sign_smul_of_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":463,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtStandardBasisCore.lean#L463-L519","doc":"**Garnir annihilation — algebraic core (sorry-free).** The sign-reversing\ninvolution at the heart of every Garnir relation. If `τ` is an involution\n(`τ*τ = 1`) of sign `-1` lying in the *row* stabiliser of `t` (so `τ` fixes the\ntabloid `{t}`), and `G` is a finite set of permutations closed under right\nmultiplication by `τ`, then the signed sum of basis tabloids\n`∑_{g∈G} sgn(g)·{g·t}` vanishes: pairing `g ↔ gτ` cancels terms, because\n`{gτ·t} = {g·t}` (`τ` fixes the row pattern) while `sgn(gτ) = -sgn(g)`.\nThis is the Mathlib-side realisation of \"the full column antisymmetriser of a\nGarnir set annihilates the tabloid\" (Sagan §2.6). It is the algebraic ingredient\nthe Garnir core (`straightening_step_colMax`, proved)\nconsumes; the pieces still missing on top of it — the coset→polytabloid\nantisymmetriser bridge (needs `CharZero k`), the Garnir-set/row-descent existence\nfor a column-word-minimal non-standard tableau, and the **column-word decrease**\n(`colWordNum (π•t) < colWordNum t`; the former `domWeight`-increase claim was FALSE —\naudit §3.5) — are recorded in the module docstring. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.polytabloid_colStab_smul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.polytabloid_colStab_smul","kind":"theorem","line":417,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtStandardBasisCore.lean#L417-L460","doc":"**Column-antisymmetry (sorry-free).** A column permutation `σ ∈ C_t` acts on\nthe polytabloid by its sign: `e_{σ·t} = sgn(σ)·e_t`. The sum over `C_{σ·t} = C_t`\nis reindexed `ρ ↦ ρσ` (right multiplication by `σ ∈ C_t`), using\n`sgn(ρσ) = sgn(ρ)sgn(σ)`, `ρ·(σ·t) = (ρσ)·t`, and `sgn(σ)² = 1`. This is the\ncolumn-sort step of Sagan §2.6: every polytabloid equals `±` its\ncolumn-standardised representative. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.colStab_smul_self","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.colStab_smul_self","kind":"theorem","line":409,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtStandardBasisCore.lean#L409-L414","doc":"For `σ ∈ C_t`, the column stabilizer is `σ`-invariant: `C_{σ·t} = C_t`.\n(`colPattern (σ·t) = σ · colPattern t = colPattern t` since `σ ∈ C_t`.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.linearIndependent_corestrict_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.linearIndependent_corestrict_iff","kind":"theorem","line":383,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtStandardBasisCore.lean#L383-L395","doc":"**Corestriction reflects independence**: independence of `standardPolytabloidS`\n(in `S^μ`) ⟺ independence of `standardPolytabloid` (in `M^μ`), since the `S^μ`\ninclusion has trivial kernel. Sorry-free. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.subtype_comp_standardPolytabloidS","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.subtype_comp_standardPolytabloidS","kind":"theorem","line":376,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtStandardBasisCore.lean#L376-L380","doc":"`(S^μ).subtype ∘ standardPolytabloidS = standardPolytabloid` (definitional). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.leadTab","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.leadTab","kind":"def","line":370,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtStandardBasisCore.lean#L370-L373","doc":"The concrete **leading-tabloid map** `lead T = {sytToTableau T}` (the row-class of\n`T`'s own filling) — the leading tabloid of `e_T`. Sorry-free. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.Triangular.linearIndependent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.Triangular.linearIndependent","kind":"theorem","line":323,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtStandardBasisCore.lean#L323-L368","doc":"**Triangular-independence lever** — the lemma the pinned Mathlib lacks, supplied\nsorry-free. A triangular `Finsupp` family (injective leading map, unit diagonal,\nsupport bounded above by the leading index) is linearly independent. Maximal-leading-\nindex argument; works over any `CommRing`. A natural Mathlib-upstream candidate.\n\nDeclared as `Triangular.linearIndependent` (not bare `linearIndependent`) because both\ncall sites consume it by dot-notation on a `Triangular` term (`htri.linearIndependent`,\nin `SpechtStandardBasis` and `SpechtFinrankWired`). The `Triangular.` prefix here is\nload-bearing, not a redundant namespace component. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.Triangular.supp_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.Triangular.supp_le","kind":"theorem","line":321,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtStandardBasisCore.lean#L321-L321","doc":"`lead i` is an upper bound of `supp (v i)` ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.Triangular.diag_unit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.Triangular.diag_unit","kind":"theorem","line":319,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtStandardBasisCore.lean#L319-L319","doc":"the diagonal coefficient is a unit ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.Triangular.lead_inj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.Triangular.lead_inj","kind":"theorem","line":317,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtStandardBasisCore.lean#L317-L317","doc":"distinct vectors have distinct leading indices ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.Triangular.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.Triangular.mk","kind":"ctor","line":314,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtStandardBasisCore.lean#L314-L314","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.Triangular","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.Triangular","kind":"structure","line":311,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtStandardBasisCore.lean#L311-L321","doc":"The triangular hypothesis bundle (upper-bound form), over any `CommRing`:\n`lead` injective, the diagonal coefficient `(v i)(lead i)` a unit, and `lead i` an\nupper bound of `supp (v i)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.exists_descent_of_not_mem_range","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.exists_descent_of_not_mem_range","kind":"theorem","line":283,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtStandardBasisCore.lean#L283-L294","doc":"**Descent existence (sorry-free).** A non-standard polytabloid comes from a tableau\nwith a row descent (right neighbour `≤`) or a column descent (lower neighbour `≤`) —\nthe contrapositive of SYT recognition. This is the entry point of the column-maximal\nGarnir core `straightening_step_colMax`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.mem_range_standardPolytabloid_of_strict","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.mem_range_standardPolytabloid_of_strict","kind":"theorem","line":271,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtStandardBasisCore.lean#L271-L280","doc":"**SYT recognition:** a tableau strict along rows and down columns has a standard\npolytabloid. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.sytToTableau_sytOfStrict","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.sytToTableau_sytOfStrict","kind":"theorem","line":248,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtStandardBasisCore.lean#L248-L268","doc":"`sytToTableau` inverts `sytOfStrict`: the honest SYT built from a strict filling\nmaps back to the original tableau. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.sytOfStrict","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.sytOfStrict","kind":"def","line":228,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtStandardBasisCore.lean#L228-L246","doc":"A `Tableau` filling that is strictly increasing along rows and down columns is an\nhonest `StandardYoungTableau`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.labelAt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.labelAt","kind":"def","line":222,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtStandardBasisCore.lean#L222-L226","doc":"The label a `Tableau μ = Fin n ≃ μ.cells` assigns to a cell `(i, j) ∈ μ` — the\n\"entry at a cell\" view, dual to `rowPattern`/`colPattern` (which report the row/column\nof a *label*): `labelAt t h = (t.symm ⟨(i,j),…⟩).val`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.standardPolytabloidS","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.standardPolytabloidS","kind":"def","line":202,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtStandardBasisCore.lean#L202-L207","doc":"The standard polytabloid **corestricted** to `S^μ` (i.e. valued in the\nsubmodule `Specht.SpechtSubmodule μ`), using `standardPolytabloid_mem`. This is\nthe family `Basis.mk` builds a basis from. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.standardPolytabloid_mem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.standardPolytabloid_mem","kind":"theorem","line":197,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtStandardBasisCore.lean#L197-L200","doc":"Every standard polytabloid lies in the Specht module (it is a polytabloid). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.standardPolytabloid","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.standardPolytabloid","kind":"def","line":190,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtStandardBasisCore.lean#L190-L194","doc":"The **standard polytabloid** `e_T = e_{sytToTableau T} ∈ M^μ` of a standard\nYoung tableau `T`. These are the candidate basis vectors of `S^μ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.sytToTableau","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.sytToTableau","kind":"def","line":182,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtStandardBasisCore.lean#L182-L186","doc":"**SYT → general tableau** (sorry-free). The bijective filling\n`Fin (nOf μ) ≃ μ.cells` reading off `T.entry`: label `l ↦` the unique cell whose\nentry is `l`. Built by inverting the bijection `cellLabel T : μ.cells ≃ Fin n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.cellLabel_bijective","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.cellLabel_bijective","kind":"theorem","line":174,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtStandardBasisCore.lean#L174-L180","doc":"`cellLabel T` is bijective: an injection between two finite types of equal\ncardinality (`card μ.cells = μ.cells.card = μ.card = nOf μ`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.instFintypeStandardYoungTableau","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.instFintypeStandardYoungTableau","kind":"instance","line":148,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtStandardBasisCore.lean#L148-L172","doc":"**`Fintype (StandardYoungTableau μ)`** — the instance brick 1 left open.\n\nAn SYT is determined by its values on `μ.cells` (off-cell entries are pinned to\n`0` by `zero_off`, and the bounds/strictness fields are `Prop`s). The map\n`T ↦ (the restricted entry function on cells)` into the *finite* function space\n`μ.cells → Fin (μ.card)` is injective, so `Fintype.ofInjective` supplies the\ninstance. (Two SYTs agreeing on every cell are equal: on-cells by the agreement,\noff-cells by `zero_off` — discharged via the `@[ext]` lemma.)\n\nThis is a **bonus**: the headline `specht_finrank_eq_numSYT` uses\n`Module.finrank_eq_nat_card_basis` (which needs no `Fintype` on the index), so\nit does not depend on this instance. Provided here to close brick 1's open\ninstance sorry-free. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.cellLabel_injective","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.cellLabel_injective","kind":"theorem","line":137,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtStandardBasisCore.lean#L137-L146","doc":"`cellLabel T` is injective: distinct cells carry distinct labels (`T.inj_on`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.cellLabel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.SpechtStandardBasis.cellLabel","kind":"def","line":132,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/SpechtStandardBasisCore.lean#L132-L135","doc":"The label that a standard tableau `T` assigns to a cell, as an element of\n`Fin (μ.card) = Fin (nOf μ)`. The bound is exactly `T.lt_card`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}